    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0697" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg655"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June
                                25,</hi>1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 16th instant, in which, after referring to the
                    recent correspondence between me and the Danish minister here, relative to the
                    use made by the United States cruisers of the port of St. Thomas, and to the
                    papers which you laid before me, with your notes of the 3d and 8th of April
                    last, in reference to the case of the Peterhoff, as well as to your note of the
                    4th ultimo, touching the proceedings of the Wachusett, in connexion with the
                    capture of the Dolphin, you address to this government a fresh and more urgent
                    remonstrance against the use made by its cruisers of the neutral port of St.
                    Thomas, and I have the honor to state, in reply, that the attention of the
                    Secretary of the Navy has been invited to it.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, your lordship’s obedient
                    servant.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
